# Groups

The one strikedown feature in this base: a `//` group directive opens a named
container, `===` splits it into sections, `// end name` closes it.

// aside

A group holding one paragraph. Ordinary markdown works the same inside a
group as outside one — `code`, **bold**, *em* all still parse.

// end aside

Two sections side by side, split by `===`:

// two

Section one.

===

Section two.

// end two

Degradation: a `//` line that doesn't parse cleanly as a directive is just a
paragraph, exactly like in any other markdown viewer.

// TODO: this line looks like a directive but isn't one — it has a colon and
a space in what would need to be the name, so it stays plain prose.

A mismatched closer degrades the same way instead of closing anything:

// example

// end nothing

// end example
